Fires that in their bosom glow;
Clouds around their cliffs dark lowering,
Torrents down their steeps that flow;

Bid the sweet blossoms their fragrance to lend;
Songs of rejoicing his footsteps attend;
Fetters are broken, the bells sweetly chime,
Crown of the victor greets glad Easter time.

Angel of Easter, so strong and so fair,
Give to the world the glad message you bear;
Lighten the pathway the victor has trod;
Earth thrills with joy at the touch of our Lord.

chorus:
